Built on the [Claude Agent SDK](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-python) using [nuvel](https://github.com/Folken2/nuvel).

## Quick start

```bash
# 1. Install
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 2. Configure
cp .env.example .env
# Add your ANTHROPIC_API_KEY

# 3. Local dev (no server)
python run_dev.py "say hello"

# 4. Server mode
python server.py
# → http://localhost:8000
# → POST /run_sse/ with {"prompt": "..."}
# → GET /health
```

## Project layout

```
{{agent_package}}/
├── agent.py              # ClaudeAgentOptions + get_client()
├── prompt/
│   └── system_prompt.md  # the system prompt (edit this)
├── tools/
│   ├── __init__.py       # tool registry → SDK MCP server
│   └── example.py        # one starter @tool — replace
├── hooks/
│   └── audit.py          # PreToolUse hook (logs every tool call)
└── traces/
    └── trace_writer.py   # writes ResultMessage to JSONL
.claude/skills/           # drop SKILL.md files here for runtime knowledge
server.py                 # FastAPI: /run_sse/, /health
run_dev.py                # local CLI for testing without server
```

## Adding a tool

Create a new module in `{{agent_package}}/tools/` with a `@tool` decorator:

```python
from claude_agent_sdk import tool

@tool("my_tool", "What this tool does", {"arg1": str})
async def my_tool(args):
    return {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "result"}]}
```

Then import it in `{{agent_package}}/tools/__init__.py` and add it to the `_TOOLS` list. Tool names exposed to Claude become `mcp__tools__my_tool`.

## Adding a skill

Drop a SKILL.md at `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with frontmatter (`name`, `description`). The SDK auto-loads it via `setting_sources=["project"]` in `agent.py`.

## Deployment

The included `Dockerfile` and `railway.json` are configured for Railway. Set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (and optionally `API_KEY` for bearer auth on `/run_sse/`) in the deployment environment.
